## ✅ WeatherCheck Flow — Built & Validated

**File:** `WeatherCheck/WeatherCheck/WeatherCheck.flow`

### What it does

```mermaid
graph LR
    trigger(Manual Trigger)
    getWeather[Get Current Weather]
    evaluate[Evaluate Weather]
    decision{Is it a nice day?}
    errorHandler[Handle Error]
    endNice(Nice Day)
    endNotNice(Not Nice Day)
    endError(Error End)
    trigger -->|output| getWeather
    getWeather -->|output| evaluate
    getWeather -->|error| errorHandler
    evaluate -->|success| decision
    decision -->|Nice day| endNice
    decision -->|Not so nice| endNotNice
    errorHandler -->|success| endError
```

### Nodes

| Node | Type | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Manual Trigger | `core.trigger.manual` | Start on demand |
| **Get Current Weather** | `uipath.connector.custom-codereval-openmeteoapis.getcurrentweather` | Calls Open-Meteo API for **Bellevue, WA** (47.6101°N, 122.2015°W) with `current_weather=true` |
| Evaluate Weather | `core.action.script` | Reads `current_weather.temperature`, `windspeed`, `weathercode`. **Nice day** = ≥ 15°C + weather code ≤ 3 (clear/partly cloudy) + wind < 30 km/h. Builds a friendly message like *"Yes! It's a nice day in Bellevue! 72°F (22°C), clear skies, wind 12 km/h."* |
| Is it a nice day? | `core.logic.decision` | Routes on `evaluateWeather1.output.isNice` |
| Nice Day / Not Nice Day / Error End | `core.control.end` | Terminal nodes for each path |
| Handle Error | `core.action.script` | Catches weather fetch failures gracefully |

